    [CI] Wait for all enabled multi-node leaders before releasing single-node (#19725)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    **Problem.** The A2 nightly gate `wait-multi-node-pods-ready` released
    the
    single-node / accuracy jobs as soon as *any* leader pod was Ready
    (`READY >= 1`),
    and it counted `role=leader` pods cluster-wide. Two issues:
    
    1. A single ready leader released single-node while the other enabled
    multi-node
    case was still starting up, so the gate did not actually wait for this
    run's
       multi-node leaders to be ready together.
    2. The global `role=leader` count could be inflated by leader pods
    outside this
    run, letting the gate release early instead of waiting on its own cases.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No end-user change; this only adjusts the internal A2 nightly CI gate.
    
    - The gate derives the expected leader set from this run's own enabled
    `config_file_path` values, using the same stem transform as the LWS name
      (drop `.yaml`, lower-case, `.`/`_` -> `-`, cap 43 chars, mirroring
      `_e2e_nightly_multi_node.yaml`), and matches the exact leader pod name
      `vllm-<stem>-<6-hex-rand>-0` rather than a loose prefix.
    - It waits until **every** enabled leader is Running + Ready (`READY >=
    EXPECTED`)
    before releasing single-node / accuracy. Multi-node tests keep running
    in the
    background in parallel; this does **not** serialize behind multi-node
    completion.
    - Readiness timeout raised from 1200s to 3600s (1h) to cover slow leader
    launch;
    the lenient fallback (warn and release anyway, do not fail the pipeline)
    is kept.
    - Scope: A2-only; no shared reusable workflow or jinja2 template is
    modified.
    
    > Note on isolation: counting by this run's config-stem prefix, together
    with the
    > tainted A2 pool (PR pods lack the matching toleration) and the
    workflow
    > `concurrency` group (`cancel-in-progress`), makes stray leaders not
    expected.
    > This is defense-in-depth rather than hard `run_id` isolation.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    This is a CI workflow shell script with no `tests/ut` harness, so the
    gate logic was
    verified offline in bash (`set -euo pipefail`) against mocked `kubectl`
    rows:
    
    - Both leaders Ready + one unrelated leader present -> `EXPECTED=2
    READY=2`,
      unrelated pod not counted.
    - Only one leader Ready, the other Pending -> `EXPECTED=2 READY=1`, gate
    holds.
    - Single-name filter -> `EXPECTED=1 READY=1`, the other case not
    counted.
    - Exact-name regex: a `foo-bar` pod does not match stem `foo`; a
    non-6-hex suffix
      is rejected.
    - YAML parses cleanly (`yaml.safe_load`); current bare-filename configs
    produce
    the same stems as before, so behavior is unchanged on the present
    matrix.
    
